# Build output only. Everything a figure depends on stays in the tree.
#
# The rule this file is written against: the rust slice's published encode column had to
# be WITHDRAWN because a `.gitignore` rule (`[Bb]in/`, meant for .NET output) swallowed its
# measurement binaries, so the commit behind its log could not be rebuilt. R4's closing
# rule is that a figure whose harness is not in the tree cannot be defended. So the
# patterns here are anchored and specific, never a bare directory name.
/build/
/core/target/
/core/target-count/
/deps/cp.txt
__pycache__/
*.pyc
